(2141779, 291606, 36999, '<td valign="top">great light and subject.  would love to see the train itself a bit sharper for the perfect pan, but very nice</td>', 'great light and subject.  would love to see the train itself a bit sharper for the perfect pan, but very nice', '2006-02-11 00:23:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141780, 291639, 47487, '<td valign="top">This is a really cute shot, very well-done, and in any other challenge would do far better than I imagine it''s doing here, because everything is (relatively) sharp. For a motion panning shot you need a slowish shutter speed, so that as you track the moving subject, the background and other stationary objects will blur. But wow, what a good-looking penguin picture.</td>', 'This is a really cute shot, very well-done, and in any other challenge would do far better than I imagine it''s doing here, because everything is (relatively) sharp. For a motion panning shot you need a slowish shutter speed, so that as you track the moving subject, the background and other stationary objects will blur. But wow, what a good-looking penguin picture.', '2006-02-11 00:23:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141783, 292775, 23002, '<td valign="top">A nice combination of motion panning and using flash to stop the action of the skier....with the shado happening after the skier i would guess this was taken with rear curtain sinc.</td>', 'A nice combination of motion panning and using flash to stop the action of the skier....with the shado happening after the skier i would guess this was taken with rear curtain sinc.', '2006-02-11 00:24:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141784, 290765, 36999, '<td valign="top">nice job but not so find of the placement of main subject</td>', 'nice job but not so find of the placement of main subject', '2006-02-11 00:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141786, 292017, 47487, '<td valign="top">Bubbleman is standing pretty still. For this to be a motion panning shot, Bubbleman would have to have been moving. Also, my eye keeps being drawn to the sharpest part of the picture, which looks to be the lwoman standing behind Bubbleman to his right.</td>', 'Bubbleman is standing pretty still. For this to be a motion panning shot, Bubbleman would have to have been moving. Also, my eye keeps being drawn to the sharpest part of the picture, which looks to be the lwoman standing behind Bubbleman to his right.', '2006-02-11 00:24:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141787, 292536, 23002, '<td valign="top">Stopping action is not the same as motion panning......</td>', 'Stopping action is not the same as motion panning......', '2006-02-11 00:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141793, 290612, 47487, '<td valign="top">JUST SAY NO TO TILT.<br/> <br/>Sorry. Personal pet peeve. Nicely done on the tracking. If the tilt was accidental, I can see your dilemma; you couldn''t rotate and crop without losint most of the blurred parts of your shot. 7 because you really truly used motion panning and did a good job of it. :) Too bad the tail end of the car is cut off.</td>', 'JUST SAY NO TO TILT. Sorry. Personal pet peeve. Nicely done on the tracking. If the tilt was accidental, I can see your dilemma; you couldn''t rotate and crop without losint most of the blurred parts of your shot. 7 because you really truly used motion panning and did a good job of it. :) Too bad the tail end of the car is cut off.', '2006-02-11 00:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2141794, 292854, 36999, '<td valign="top">very nice</td>', 'very nice', '2006-02-11 00:26:22.000000', NULL, 1),
