(2160415, 291067, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"High Jump Commences" fits perfectly into the Motion Panning challenge.   Not too bad of a placement or score, this was a though challenge.  <br/> <br/>I really think the most important and best aspect of your shot is the focal point being his face.  You have captured so much of what makes us human by allowing the focus to be his determination.  The blur is nice and shows the fast past movement. I think it the shot would have scored a little higher if there were no other people in the background, but I am sure this was a hard enough shot to take.  Also I think you took a brave step with adding such a thick border but it really works for me.  The only other thing I would try would be to increase the contrast some jus to make the shot brighter.   Great work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "High Jump Commences" fits perfectly into the Motion Panning challenge.   Not too bad of a placement or score, this was a though challenge.   I really think the most important and best aspect of your shot is the focal point being his face.  You have captured so much of what makes us human by allowing the focus to be his determination.  The blur is nice and shows the fast past movement. I think it the shot would have scored a little higher if there were no other people in the background, but I am sure this was a hard enough shot to take.  Also I think you took a brave step with adding such a thick border but it really works for me.  The only other thing I would try would be to increase the contrast some jus to make the shot brighter.   Great work.', '2006-02-18 01:24:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2161808, 290777, 41918, '<td valign="top">Cracking shot!<br/> <br/>I agree with the comments about the tree - although I realise this isn''t always the easiest thing to do on the fly...<br/> <br/>I wonder whether this would have benefitted from a slightly lower viewpoint? Also not too sure about the square (?) crop - but I don''t know what you may have wanted to crop out of the image. Just my 5 eggs worth...<br/> <br/>I love the reflection on the spokes - it really helps to portray the speed element. And the panning and focus seem spot on.<br/>More like this please!<br/> <br/> <br/> <br/>EDIT for clarity<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-18 18:36:43.</i></td>', 'Cracking shot! I agree with the comments about the tree - although I realise this isn''t always the easiest thing to do on the fly... I wonder whether this would have benefitted from a slightly lower viewpoint? Also not too sure about the square (?) crop - but I don''t know what you may have wanted to crop out of the image. Just my 5 eggs worth... I love the reflection on the spokes - it really helps to portray the speed element. And the panning and focus seem spot on.More like this please!   EDIT for clarity', '2006-02-18 18:36:12.000000', '2006-02-18 18:36:43.000000', 0),
