(2168458, 292749, 52861, '<td valign="top">I want to thank everyone for all the good commentaries, and I totally accept that this picture should''ve been in an Abstract contest instead. <br/> <br/>Personally I love it, but it doesn''t follow all the Motion Panning rules.<br/> <br/>Thanks and Congratulation to the winners. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-21 15:49:44.</i></td>', 'I want to thank everyone for all the good commentaries, and I totally accept that this picture should''ve been in an Abstract contest instead.  Personally I love it, but it doesn''t follow all the Motion Panning rules. Thanks and Congratulation to the winners. :)', '2006-02-21 15:49:02.000000', '2006-02-21 15:49:44.000000', 0),
(2168725, 291376, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique club:<br/>The reason for the low score is probably because people wanted to see something moving and the background blured. I find the background a bit distracting. A simple black backround could have made this picture much better. Or maby if you would have taken out the white stuff between the keyboard and the monitor. But man am I thirsty for a beer right now! Good luck in future challanges. You''ve got some interesting shots in your portfolio. I liked your abstract shot! Great bw. Best wishes, arnit</td>', 'Critique club:The reason for the low score is probably because people wanted to see something moving and the background blured. I find the background a bit distracting. A simple black backround could have made this picture much better. Or maby if you would have taken out the white stuff between the keyboard and the monitor. But man am I thirsty for a beer right now! Good luck in future challanges. You''ve got some interesting shots in your portfolio. I liked your abstract shot! Great bw. Best wishes, arnit', '2006-02-21 18:22:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2169280, 292140, 49480, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>Hard to say much about this photo.  It was an interesting submission for this challenge.  The lighting is strange with the bright stripe behind you and there''s a large shadow across your face.  The long exposure made your face distort which is distracting.  I think you probably could''ve achieved what you were looking for here with a shorter exposure which would have resulted in less ''deformation.''  I think this didn''t score well because nothing is jumping out of the picture.  The idea behind motion panning is to blur the background to give a look of speed to the subject and bring the subject out of the shot.  Here, you''re blurred too (because it''s hard to stay still in the frame) so it''s basically just an interesting study in motion panning as opposed to a picture that makes people really interested in the subject.  Very clever idea though and definitely very interesting.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Hard to say much about this photo.  It was an interesting submission for this challenge.  The lighting is strange with the bright stripe behind you and there''s a large shadow across your face.  The long exposure made your face distort which is distracting.  I think you probably could''ve achieved what you were looking for here with a shorter exposure which would have resulted in less ''deformation.''  I think this didn''t score well because nothing is jumping out of the picture.  The idea behind motion panning is to blur the background to give a look of speed to the subject and bring the subject out of the shot.  Here, you''re blurred too (because it''s hard to stay still in the frame) so it''s basically just an interesting study in motion panning as opposed to a picture that makes people really interested in the subject.  Very clever idea though and definitely very interesting.', '2006-02-21 22:48:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2175301, 292796, 75713, '<td valign="top">Just going back over the photos I rated really high (9) to see how they did...... This was one of my very fav shots - I don''t give 9''s lightly - I think it should have ribboned - I can only imagine the pride that young guy will feel when you give him a copy of this unique/excellent action shot</td>', 'Just going back over the photos I rated really high (9) to see how they did...... This was one of my very fav shots - I don''t give 9''s lightly - I think it should have ribboned - I can only imagine the pride that young guy will feel when you give him a copy of this unique/excellent action shot', '2006-02-23 08:31:35.000000', NULL, 0),
